{"type":"standard","title":"Idakho-Isukha-Tiriki language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Idakho-Isukha-Tiriki language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q12952512","titles":{"canonical":"Idakho-Isukha-Tiriki_language","normalized":"Idakho-Isukha-Tiriki language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Idakho-Isukha-Tiriki language</span></span>"},"pageid":35328793,"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1347799740","tid":"01974e21-3396-11f1-88a8-7682b60d9162","timestamp":"2026-04-08T21:57:59Z","description":"Bantu dialect group of Kenya","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idakho-Isukha-Tiriki_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idakho-Isukha-Tiriki_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idakho-Isukha-Tiriki_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Idakho-Isukha-Tiriki_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idakho-Isukha-Tiriki_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Idakho-Isukha-Tiriki_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idakho-Isukha-Tiriki_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Idakho-Isukha-Tiriki_language"}},"extract":"Idakho, Isukha, and Tiriki are dialects of a Kenyan language within the Luhya ethnic group. They are a set of languages closely related to some other Luhya ethnic groups like Maragoli, but less so in comparison to others, like Bukusu, Tachoni or Samia.","extract_html":"<p><b>Idakho</b>, <b>Isukha</b>, and <b>Tiriki</b> are dialects of a Kenyan language within the Luhya ethnic group. They are a set of languages closely related to some other Luhya ethnic groups like Maragoli, but less so in comparison to others, like Bukusu, Tachoni or Samia.</p>"}